\page mouse Mouse

It is sometimes easier to control a user interface with mouse actions rather than the sole keyboard. Luckily, most of the 
terminal emulators support mouse features.

Below table describes different mouse support modes in the Nocterm library:

| Feature                        | Description                         |
| ------------------------------ | ----------------------------------- |
| NOCTERM_MOUSE_SUPPORT_NONE     | Mouse support is disabled (Default) |
| NOCTERM_MOUSE_SUPPORT_SIMPLE   | Classic mouse actions are allowed   |
| NOCTERM_MOUSE_SUPPORT_ADVANCED | Classic + advanced features         |

To set the current mouse support, call the `nocterm_mouse_set_support()` before calling the `nocterm_init()` function. 

